CodeRabbit #291 (Major): the tier was "proposed at gate.intent" yet the Lean tier
could disable gate.intent — making the proposal checkpoint unreachable — and the
section conflated repo-wide gate toggles with per-issue gate events. Now: the tier
proposal is a plain conversational checkpoint (never itself a gate, always
reachable); the per-issue tier decides which enabled gates smith requires for THIS
issue; `forge gate enable|disable` is the separate repo-wide default. Canonical +
regenerated mirror.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
